# IRON floor for generated ARTIFACTS: the oldest IRON commit a staged decode/prefill ELF may have
# been generated by. install.sh gates every staged artifact's meta.json `iron.commit` on it.
#
# This is a POLICY, not a derivation. It names the oldest IRON we are willing to ship artifacts
# from, and it moves only when an IRON defect is found that silently changes emitted bytes.
#
# Deliberately NOT a key in toolchain.lock: that file's content IS the freshness hash every
# artifact is stamped with (install.sh's staged_pin, kernel_registry::current_toolchain_hash), so
# a line there would restamp every artifact and force a full rebuild to bump a floor.
#
# bc280c2, 2026-09-20 -- "gemv: group reuse wrote C batch-major while the core emits tile-major".
# A coalesced group-reuse GEMV's C tap walked the batch axis outermost while the core emits
# tile-major, so only the b == t diagonal landed. On the gemma4-12b 256k arms that is output tile
# 0 of each column: correct through position 2047, digit garbage from 2048. Nothing else could see
# it -- toolchain hash, arena pairing, ELF size to within 16 bytes and sequence_name were all
# identical between the build carrying the defect and the build without it.
